{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1045364-supernatural-retainers","id":1045364,"title":"Supernatural Retainers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-07T13:56:52-08:00","id":1045364,"title":"Supernatural Retainers","content":"Alright, so we already had a discussion of how the Retainer Merit can denote any type of creature, from animals to mages. I like this idea a lot, using it instead of stating out various characters and followers.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut major templates who use their supernatural abilities are not limited to max 10 dice on a die roll because they often add a powerstat or similar to the equation, making their supernatural rolls potentially 15 dice. Would it work to say that a supernatural entity when rolling for a supernatural action such as activating a werewolf Gift or casting a spell use a dice pool of 3 times their Retainer rating?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:06:17-08:00","id":1045373,"title":"","content":"I would not allow it. <br /> <br /> We do have rules, such as Cruac Styles, that modify Retainer and give them supernatural powers that boost the usual dice rolls from Retainer. As well, &quot;supernatural nature&quot; is usually the justification for having 4 or 5 dot retainers in the first place. <br /> <br /> As well, a Retainer's area of expertise does not match up to having magical powers nicely 1-for-1 all the time. For instance, a Mehket vampire Retainer geared towards being just a socialite is going to be getting some very odd results from this rule. Better off to just mark the powers down separately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T21:02:04-08:00","id":1045594,"title":"","content":"Honestly, if you're developing a character that in-depth that the nuance of powerstat in a supernatural ability activation is important you should basically just go the whole hog and develop them as a fully statted NPC to have actual explicit relationships with your characters.<br /> <br /> 10 dice is an enormous dicepool regardless (assuming proficiency) while 5 dice is a great pool for most actions. For characters that are supposed to represent bit players, this is well adequate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T22:27:40-08:00","id":1045621,"title":"","content":"The whole point of using simple, abstract stats for Retainers is so you don't have to quibble over details like dice pools for specific powers. 10 dice is plenty for a 5 dot retainer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:55:32-08:00","id":1045796,"title":"","content":"Alright then, I bow to your wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}